      "criteriaText": "Company Overview Sagacious IP is the world’s largest IP research firm that provides reliable support to the worldwide IP community, including large corporations, small and mid-size corporations, IP law firms, licensing firms, and universities. The company offers patent information and searching services, patent licensing and monetization, patent analytics, patent drafting support, trademark search and watch, and patent paralegal support. Sagacious IP has over 500 full-time employees and serves over 5,000 clients from 60+ countries. The company prides itself on attracting and nurturing the industry’s finest talent across the globe. Role Summary We are seeking a dynamic and passionate individual to join the Information and Communication Technology (ICT) Searching & Analytics team at Sagacious IP. This is an excellent opportunity to collaborate with some of the most innovative researchers in the Intellectual Property Rights (IPR) industry. If you are enthusiastic about making meaningful contributions in this field, we encourage you to seize this opportunity and apply. Key Responsibilities Areas Patent Monetization: 1. Providing Licensing Support to assist companies against their competitors. 2. Developing Evidence of Use (EOU)/Claim Charts to assist with infringement lawsuits. 3. Conducting patent portfolio analysis to assist with acquisition. Patent Searching: 1. Performing Invalidation Searches to support defendants in infringement lawsuits. 2. Conducting Freedom-to-Operate (FTO) Searches to help companies launch new products/services. 3. Executing Patentability Searches to assist companies in filing new patents. Technology Landscapes: 1. Conducting White Space Analysis to understand complete technology landscape. 2. Performing Competitor Monitoring to help companies understand their competitors’ technological directions. Within these projects, the primary responsibilities include: 1. Ensuring the performance and comprehensiveness of various patent searches. 2. Efficienctly conducting comprehensive searches of technical and patent information using online database and other information resources. 3. Analyzing and summarizing of search results. 4. Providing insightful evaluation and analysis of results. 5. Preparing final reports and deliverables as per required standards. 6. Delivering timely, value-added patent search reports. An individual working as a senior patent analyst is expected to have a thorough technical understanding since their work would be presented to Chief IP Counsels, Patent Attorneys, Inventors, Patent Engineers, etc. The candidate should have good command over the English language, as they are expected to handle projects independently from end to end. Desired Work Experience 2-5 years Desired Educational Qualifications B.Tech/M.Tech in ECE/CSE/IT Compensation As per company standards Apply Now",
